      "summary": "Bug/profile load recovery (#1636)",
      "description": "* Move delayed button arming into ShowCompactConfirmation, fix color flash\n\nThe preset delete confirmation disabled its confirm button after the\ndialog was shown, which flashed the button's enabled color for a frame:\nthe button's color-tint transition lerps to the disabled color over its\nfade duration instead of switching instantly.\n\nShowCompactConfirmation now takes an armDelaySeconds parameter that\ndisables the confirm button fade-free before it first renders and\nre-enables it (with its given color restored) after the delay. Preset\ndeletion collapses to a single call with armDelaySeconds: 2.\n\n* Recover from invalid profile records instead of failing the whole load\n\nLoading profiles previously deserialized the entire JSON array in one\ncall, so a single unrecognized record threw and prevented every profile\nfrom loading; the backup path had the same flaw, and PlayerContainer\nwas never left initialized, so new profiles could not be saved either.\n\n- Parse the profile array element-by-element and register each record in\n  its own failure boundary, so valid profiles survive invalid neighbors.\n- Fall back to the backup only when the main file is not structurally\n  readable; a partially valid main file keeps its valid records.\n- Always initialize the container on non-throwing paths (even with zero\n  valid profiles) and refresh bindings, which already skips orphans.\n- Records this version cannot load are set aside in a sidecar file\n  (profiles.json.unloaded) with the version that last tried them,\n  preserved verbatim and never deleted automatically; on later loads\n  under a different version they are retried and promoted on success.\n- Guard registration against null records, duplicate IDs, and migration\n  failures, skipping only the offending record.\n- Preserve structurally unreadable sources as profiles.json.invalid\n  (timestamped if one exists) before any sanitized rewrite.\n- Show one aggregate warning toast with the skipped-record count;\n  per-record details go to the log.\n\n* Show set-aside profiles in the profile list\n\nRecords this version could not load now appear under a 'Couldn't Load'\ngroup in the profile list, rendered with the existing profile row\nprefab in an inert mode: the name is shown with a 'could not be\nloaded by this version of YARG' suffix, connect/disconnect and\nreorder controls are hidden or disabled, and selecting the row shows\nnothing in the sidebar. The row's delete button removes the record\nfrom the sidecar after a delayed-confirmation dialog.\n\nBot deletion gains the same delayed-confirmation dialog (it was\npreviously instant with no prompt); regular profile deletion is\nunchanged. All delete paths now refresh the list so emptied group\nheaders disappear immediately."
    },
